<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco changes bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco changes bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has lifted A-960 bunker fuel prices from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $1 to $104.50 a tonne ($16.04 a barrel) with effect May 15, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-960 from the Red Sea ports of Jeddah and Yanbu is $2 lower at $98 a tonne ($15.04).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the two Gulf ports is $0.50 lower at $211.50 a tonne and $4.50 higher from the Red Sea at $197.</p>
</text>
